"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T07:11:19-07:00","id":1450953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1450869-bonds-core-aeon-aberrant-adventure?p=1450906#post1450906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've used them a couple of times. They can give the characters a little boost here and there. Most of the time I forget about the mechanics and forget to call for the rolls when it would make sense. I ran a session where the party was sent on an all expenses paid vacation and some party members developed various bonds over that session. Most of those were promptly cashed in over the next couple of sessions. But, it did make the player's relationships to some of the NPCs come to the fore.<br /> <br /> TLDR: They can be fun, but are often forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Since I've only read the rules and couldn't try them in practice yet, I'm trying to understand how they feel in actual play. I'd love to know what other players felt!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}